{"raw": {"https://otago.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600772": {"title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer/Associate Professor", "description": "Job Description - Lecturer/Senior Lecturer/Associate Professor - Prosthodontics (2600772) Go to the main content section. Human Resources Information for Staff Working @ Otago Join Otago About Otago University Application toolkit Living & working in New Zealand Career development & training Health & Safety HR toolkit HR policies Contacts & enquiries Current Vacancies Otago staff should use the internal version Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Jobs | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Job Page Basic Search | Advanced Search | Jobs Matching My Profile | All Jobs Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Lecturer/Senior Lecturer/Associate Professor - Prosthodontics (2600772) Lecturer/Senior Lecturer/Associate Professor - Prosthodontics - 2600772 __________ DEPARTMENT OF ORAL REHABILITATION FACULTY OF DENTISTRY | TE KAUPEKA P\u016aNIHO Who we are | Ko wai m\u0101tou The University of Otago is one of New Zealand\u2019s largest and most research-intensive universities. Founded in 1907, the Faculty of Dentistry is based at the University\u2019s main campus in Dunedin and is the only dental school in New Zealand. It is proud of its international reputation for research, clinical, and academic excellence. The 2026 QS World University Subject Rankings list the Dental School as 50th in the world. We are committed to working closely with iwi and M\u0101ori organisations, and m\u0101tauraka M\u0101ori has become an integral part of teaching and research across the institution. We especially value our relationship with Ngai Tahu, the mana whenua within their takiw\u0101 of Te Waipounamu, and the University\u2019s principal Treaty partner. The role | Te mahi The Faculty of Dentistry seeks to appoint a Lecturer/Senior Lecturer/Associate Professor in Prosthodontics. This position provides an excellent opportunity for an academic to establish themselves in one of the leading dental schools in the world. Key tasks for this position include: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Delivering clinical teaching at undergraduate and postgraduate levels. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Contributing to curriculum design for undergraduate and postgraduate levels. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Supervising undergraduate and postgraduate research. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Undertaking research resulting in quality-assured publications within the discipline, either individually or as part of a group. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Contributing to the running of the Department, School, Division and the University. You will be supported through a collegial academic environment, an active and dynamic research culture, and through efficient professional services across the University. The Faculty is housed in modern, state-of the art facilities. Academic, research and clinical activities are centred around the Walsh Building and Clinical Services Building in Dunedin, with an additional satellite clinic in Auckland. Your skills and experience | K\u0101 p\u016bkeka me k\u0101 wheako The successful applicant will hold a dental degree and a specialist qualification in Prosthodontics, preferably also a higher research degree (PhD or equivalent), and will demonstrate: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0A track record or potential of internationally peer-reviewed research. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Teaching skills at undergraduate and postgraduate levels. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Ability to provide specialist patient care. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0A collaborative and collegial approach to work. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Full understanding of the principles of the Treaty of Waitangi and the University\u2019s M\u0101ori Strategic Framework. You will be a dentist who is registerable with the Dental Council of New Zealand in the specialist scope of Prosthodontics. Further details | P\u016broko This is a permanent, full-time (1.0 FTE) position based in \u014ctepoti/Dunedin. The salary range for this position is (per annum): \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Lecturer $98,583 to $120,528 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Senior Lecturer $148,416 to $184,993 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Associate Professor $195,968 to $212,427 The University of Otago is known for collegiality and combined with living in the vibrant city of Dunedin, provides opportunities for an excellent work-life balance. The Dunedin campus has been ranked as one of the 15 most beautiful in the world. The city has affordable living, excellent schools, and a great array of activities, ranging from art and literature to outdoor activities. The University is committed to meeting its obligations under the Children Act 2014. Candidates who successfully make the final stages of the recruitment process will be required to undergo a safety check. For further information, please contact Farai Madambi, Senior Recruitment Consultant via the email address below. Application | Tono Candidates are requested to submit the following: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0CV \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Cover letter \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Names and email addresses of at least three referees. To submit your application, please click the apply button below. Applications quoting reference number 2600772 will close on Sunday, 11 October 2026. Additional Information Contact: Farai Madambi Position details: Information Statement Guidelines for Academic Positions: Guidelines Further Information: Department Website Create an email with a link to this vacancy: Create email Location: About Dunedin Primary Location NZL-SI-Dunedin Employment Status Permanent Salary Level and Range Please see information above Organisation Oral Rehabilitation Job Function Teaching ^ Top of page | Accessibility | Copyright & Disclaimer | Contact Us | Feedback | Top of page \u00a9 Human Resources 1st Floor Registry Building PO Box 56 Dunedin 9054 New Zealand Tel 64 3 479 8269 Fax 64 3 479 8279 Email human.resources@otago.ac.nz"}, "https://otago.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600967": {"title": "Graduate Dentist Intern (Dunedin/Auckland)", "description": "Job Description - Graduate Dentist Intern (Dunedin/Auckland) (2600967) Go to the main content section. Human Resources Information for Staff Working @ Otago Join Otago About Otago University Application toolkit Living & working in New Zealand Career development & training Health & Safety HR toolkit HR policies Contacts & enquiries Current Vacancies Otago staff should use the internal version Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Jobs | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Job Page Basic Search | Advanced Search | Jobs Matching My Profile | All Jobs Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Graduate Dentist Intern (Dunedin/Auckland) (2600967) Graduate Dentist Intern (Dunedin/Auckland) - 2600967 __________ CLINICAL SERVICES FACULTY OF DENTISTRY | TE KAUPEKA P\u016aNIHO Are you a new or recent dental graduate seeking an exciting opportunity to join a supportive culture founded on teamwork, integrity, and social responsibility? We are looking for passionate and driven graduate dentists to join our modern team based dental practice at our facilities in \u014ctepoti, Dunedin and T\u0101maki Makaurau, Auckland. The role | Te mahi The Faculty of Dentistry invites applications for up to four full-time fixed term positions across both campuses with the possibility of three positions in \u014ctepoti, Dunedin and one position in T\u0101maki Makaurau, Auckland, commencing 2027. In these roles you will work with experienced clinicians to provide a wide scope of general dental procedures including urgent care. Throughout this placement, you can benefit from ongoing mentoring, training, support, and coaching. These early career positions offer a unique opportunity where you can have the ability to gain valuable clinical experience under the mentorship of experienced dentists and academics within the Faculty of Dentistry, University of Otago. You can build and enhance your clinical skills in a culturally supportive environment that includes dental treatment delivering planned treatments and urgent care. Your skills and experience | K\u0101 p\u016bkeka me k\u0101 wheako We seek Dentists within their first three years of working, who could value interacting with other professionals and who thrive on working in a supportive environment founded on teamwork, integrity, and social responsibility. You aspire to form a firm foundation of clinical skills and there can be opportunities to get involved in teaching, research, or postgraduate learning. To be successful in this role, you should also have: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Strong knowledge and understanding in all areas of general dentistry. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Exceptional communication and patient care skills. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0An ability to work in a large cohesive team environment. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Outstanding time management and organisational skills. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0A strong desire to consolidate your clinical skills in a supportive environment. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0An ability to provide high quality dental care to all age groups of patients. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0A drive to support students as a mentor in areas commensurate with your clinical expertise. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Knowledge or the ability to acquire knowledge of procedures, policies, regulations and standards of practice. Applicants must be registered or registrable with the Dental Council of New Zealand (DCNZ). Further details | Puroko We have multiple, full-time (1 FTE), fixed term (18 January 2027 \u2013 14 January 2028) positions, located in \u014ctepoti, Dunedin or T\u0101maki Makaurau, Auckland. The salary for these positions is $79,812 per annum. You must have the right to live and work in New Zealand to apply for this job. For further information, please contact Yolin Govender (Auckland) or Pip MacDonald (Dunedin) via the contact details below. Application | Tono To submit your application (including CV and cover letter) please click the apply button. Applications quoting reference number 2600967 will close on Sunday, 27 September 2026. Applications may be considered as they are received. The University reserves the right to close this vacancy at any time. Additional Information Contact: Yolin Govender (Auckland) Contact: Pip MacDonald (Dunedin) Position details: Information Statement Guidelines for Academic Positions: Guidelines Further Information: Department Website Create an email with a link to this vacancy: Create email Location: About Dunedin Primary Location NZL-SI-Dunedin Employment Status Fixed Term Salary Level and Range The University is offering a remuneration level commensurate with the responsibilities of the position. Organisation Clinical Services Job Function Teaching ^ Top of page | Accessibility | Copyright & Disclaimer | Contact Us | Feedback | Top of page \u00a9 Human Resources 1st Floor Registry Building PO Box 56 Dunedin 9054 New Zealand Tel 64 3 479 8269 Fax 64 3 479 8279 Email human.resources@otago.ac.nz"}, "https://otago.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=2501589": {"title": "Senior Professional Practice Fellow", "description": "Job Description - Senior Professional Practice Fellow - Dentistry (2501589) Go to the main content section. Human Resources Information for Staff Working @ Otago Join Otago About Otago University Application toolkit Living & working in New Zealand Career development & training Health & Safety HR toolkit HR policies Contacts & enquiries Current Vacancies Otago staff should use the internal version Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Jobs | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Job Page Basic Search | Advanced Search | Jobs Matching My Profile | All Jobs Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Senior Professional Practice Fellow - Dentistry (2501589) Senior Professional Practice Fellow - Dentistry - 2501589 __________ DIVISION OF HEALTH SCIENCES | TE W\u0100HANGA MATUA M\u0100TAU HAUORA FACULTY OF DENTISTRY | TE KAUPEKA P\u016aNIHO Who we are | Ko wai m\u0101tou The University of Otago is one of New Zealand\u2019s largest and most research-intensive universities. Founded in 1907, the Faculty of Dentistry is based at the University\u2019s main campus in Dunedin with clinics in Auckland and South Dunedin and is the only dental school in New Zealand. We are proud of our international reputation for research, clinical, and academic excellence. The 2023 QS World University Subject Rankings list the Dental School as 42nd in the world. The Faculty of Dentistry comprises of three Departments (Oral Rehabilitation, Oral Diagnostic and Surgical and Oral Sciences) as well as the Sir John Walsh Research Institute. Dunedin offers an outstanding quality of life, combining the vibrancy of a university city with the warmth of a close-knit community. The region provides exceptional schooling and educational opportunities, making it an ideal place for families. Dunedin is perfectly placed for outdoor pursuits, with world-class mountain bike trails, nearby ski fields, and excellent surfing. Just a few hours from Queenstown\u2014the adventure capital of New Zealand\u2014it also offers easy access to some of the country\u2019s most stunning natural landscapes. Dunedin\u2019s wildlife is world-renowned, home to the royal albatross, seals, penguins, and an array of native birds. \u2018The outdoors and wildlife was one of our biggest pulls to this area as a family coming from the UK - also the schools are fantastic!\u2019 \u00a0H. Smith, Senior Professional Practice Fellow. The role | Te mahi The University is seeking applications from suitably qualified candidates for the position of Senior Professional Practice Fellows in Dentistry. As a Senior Professional Practice Fellow, you will help support teaching, facilitate learning, assist with assessments, and carry out clinical service/clinical activity both on undergraduate clinics and staff clinics out of term time. Some key tasks of the role include: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Clinical teaching/tutoring of undergraduate dentists. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Contributing to the Department\u2019s academic goals by applying expert clinical knowledge in your area of specialty. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Preparation, assessment, teaching and paper administration duties. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Following through patient care and referrals within the hospital. Your skills and experience | K\u0101 p\u016bkeka me k\u0101 wheako Successful applicants: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Must hold a dental degree and have registration or be eligible for full registration with the Dental Council of New Zealand. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Will demonstrate the ability to work well with students and staff from differing academic and cultural backgrounds and at all levels within the institution. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Show a commitment to uphold the principles of the Treaty of Waitangi and the University\u2019s M\u0101ori Strategic Framework. Candidates will also have and maintain registration (if supervised) including: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0A practicing certificate in place before starting work. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Indemnity in place prior to starting work. Further details | P\u016broko We have eight job openings, offering both permanent and fixed-term positions, located in \u014ctepoti, Dunedin. We have opportunities for Dentists with special interests in Endodontics, Prosthodontics and Periodontics. Both full-time (1 FTE) and part-time positions are available, allowing for employment over the full year or semester time only. The duration of any fixed-term positions can be negotiable with the successful candidates. International candidates would need to be available to work minimum 0.8FTE. The salary range for these positions is $109,554 to $184,993 per annum (pro rata). Candidates will be appointed to a step on the Senior Professional Practice Fellow scale 3 or 4, dependent on qualifications and skills. The University is committed to meeting its obligations under the Children\u2019s Act 2014. \u00a0Candidates who successfully make the final stages of the recruitment process will be required to undergo a safety check. Specific enquiries about this position may be directed to Dr Pip MacDonald via the contact details below. Application | Tono Candidates are requested to submit the following: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0CV. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Cover letter. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Names and email addresses of at least three referees. To submit your application, please click the apply button. Applications should quote reference number 2501598. There is no formal closing date for this role. We may begin interviewing suitable candidates at any \u00a0time during the recruitment process and reserve the right to make an appointment before the advertised closing date. LI-DNI Additional Information Contact: Dr Pip MacDonald Position details: Information Statement Guidelines for Academic Positions: Guidelines Further Information: Department Website & Faculty of Dentistry Video Tour Create an email with a link to this vacancy: Create email Location: About Dunedin Primary Location NZL-SI-Dunedin Employment Status Permanent Salary Level and Range Senior Teaching & Professional Practice Fellow - Medical & Dental 3 ($109,554 to $120,528) or 4 ($148,414 to $184,993) Organisation Office of the Head of Faculty (Dentistry) Job Function Teaching ^ Top of page | Accessibility | Copyright & Disclaimer | Contact Us | Feedback | Top of page \u00a9 Human Resources 1st Floor Registry Building PO Box 56 Dunedin 9054 New Zealand Tel 64 3 479 8269 Fax 64 3 479 8279 Email human.resources@otago.ac.nz"}, "https://otago.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=2601312": {"title": "Senior Teaching Fellow", "description": "Job Description - Senior Teaching Fellow -  Psychological Medicine  (2601312) Go to the main content section. Human Resources Information for Staff Working @ Otago Join Otago About Otago University Application toolkit Living & working in New Zealand Career development & training Health & Safety HR toolkit HR policies Contacts & enquiries Current Vacancies Otago staff should use the internal version Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Jobs | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Job Page Basic Search | Advanced Search | Jobs Matching My Profile | All Jobs Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Senior Teaching Fellow -  Psychological Medicine  (2601312) Senior Teaching Fellow -  Psychological Medicine - 2601312 __________ DEPARTMENT OF PSYCHOLOGICAL MEDICINE, DUNEDIN | TE TARI WHAKAORA HINENGARO TANGATA DUNEDIN SCHOOL OF MEDICINE | TE KURA WHAIORA A \u014cTEPOTI The Role | Te mahi The Department of Psychological Medicine (Dunedin) advances psychological medicine through the integration of academic and clinical expertise in psychiatry, clinical psychology, and health psychology. We are seeking a Teaching Fellow to contribute to teaching within the MB ChB programme, and the Royal Australian and New Zealand College\u2019s Formal Education Course, Registrar programme, in 2027. This position will play an important role in supporting the delivery and ongoing development of the curriculum, helping to equip future medical graduates with the knowledge, skills, and professional capabilities required to work effectively in the field of psychological medicine. The role includes convening responsibilities for the Year 6 programme and the Registrar Teaching programme, along with supporting teaching, assessment, and curriculum initiatives across the Department. Key responsibilities include: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Convening responsibilities \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Supporting the development and delivery of course materials. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Assisting with the administration and coordination of the MB ChB programme and Registrar programme. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Collaborating with academic teaching and research staff \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Supporting strategic projects and initiatives that enhance teaching and curriculum development. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Contributing to assessment activities and associated administration. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Assisting with teaching-related operational and documentation requirements. Skills and Experience | K\u0101 p\u016bkeka me k\u0101 wheako To be successful in this role, you will have: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0A medical qualification (eligible to work in NZ) as a Consultant Psychiatrist. We would consider Senior Psychiatric Registrars who are close to completing their fellowship. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Teaching experience in the field of psychological medicine (preferable) \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Strong organisational and administrative skills. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0The ability to work effectively both independently and collaboratively. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0A commitment to Te Tiriti o Waitangi, equity, diversity, and inclusion. Further Details | P\u016broko The Department is seeking to fill a total of 0.4 FTE (15 hours per week) and is open to appointing either: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0One candidate at 0.4 FTE, or \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Two candidates at 0.2 FTE (7.5 hours per week each). This is a fixed-term position from the 7th of December 2026 for the Registrar convening role, or the 18 January 2027, for the MB ChB Year 6 convening role, to 28 January 2028, based in \u014ctepoti, Dunedin. The salary for this position will be based on the successful candidate's skills, experience, and qualifications and is expected to fall within the range of Senior Teaching & Professional Practice Fellow Practice Fellow - $109,554 to $120,528 or $148,414 to $184,993 (pro rata). The University of Otago is a workplace that values and celebrates diverse and inclusive thinking, people, and behaviours. We are committed to fostering an environment where staff from a wide range of backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives feel valued, respected, and supported to succeed. You must have the right to live and work in New Zealand to apply for this position. Confidential enquiries regarding the role may be directed to Associate Professor Tess Patterson via the contact details below. Application | Tono To submit your application, please click the apply button and include your CV and cover letter. Applications quoting reference number 2601312 will close on Sunday, 18 October 2026. Additional Information Note: As a part-time position, the salary range for this role will be the pro-rata equivalent of the annual full-time salary range listed. Contact: Associate Professor Tess Patterson Position details: Information Statement Guidelines for Academic Positions: Guidelines Further Information: Department Website Create an email with a link to this vacancy: Create email Location: About Dunedin Primary Location NZL-SI-Dunedin Employment Status Fixed Term Salary Level and Range Senior Teaching & Professional Practice Fellow - Medical & Dental 3 ($109,554 to $120,528) or 4 ($148,414 to $184,993) Organisation Psychological Medicine Job Function Teaching ^ Top of page | Accessibility | Copyright & Disclaimer | Contact Us | Feedback | Top of page \u00a9 Human Resources 1st Floor Registry Building PO Box 56 Dunedin 9054 New Zealand Tel 64 3 479 8269 Fax 64 3 479 8279 Email human.resources@otago.ac.nz"}, "https://otago.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=2601264": {"title": "College of Education Children's Writer in Residence for 2027", "description": "Job Description - College of Education Children's Writer in Residence for 2027 (2601264) Go to the main content section. Human Resources Information for Staff Working @ Otago Join Otago About Otago University Application toolkit Living & working in New Zealand Career development & training Health & Safety HR toolkit HR policies Contacts & enquiries Current Vacancies Otago staff should use the internal version Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Jobs | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Job Page Basic Search | Advanced Search | Jobs Matching My Profile | All Jobs Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - College of Education Children's Writer in Residence for 2027 (2601264) College of Education Children's Writer in Residence for 2027 - 2601264 __________ Applications are invited for the College of Education Children's Writer in Residence for 2027 Applications are invited for the 2027 residency from children\u2019s writers who usually reside in Aotearoa New Zealand. Begun by the Dunedin College of Education in 1992, the College of Education Children\u2019s Writer in Residence, has allowed children\u2019s writers to write full time in a compatible environment among colleagues who are involved with the teaching of reading and literature to children. \u00a0The financial support and imaginative space the residency afford has enabled writers to create a huge variety and number of books for New Zealand\u2019s young readers. With support from Creative New Zealand to fund the writer\u2019s remuneration, the residency is offered in partnership with the Robert Lord Writers Cottage Trust, which provides rent-free accommodation to writers in the historic Titan Street cottage bequeathed by the late playwright Robert Lord. What the Residency offers \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0A 14-week full-time position (February 2027). \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0A stipend equivalent to a University Lecturer\u2019s salary (pro-rata), less the value of accommodation provided at the Robert Lord Writers Cottage. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Furnished accommodation, including wireless broadband internet access at the Robert Lord Writers Cottage. \u00a0Excludes power costs. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0A dedicated writing office on campus within College of Education. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Access to the University Library and wider University community. Who can apply Writers who are normally resident in New Zealand. A degree or formal qualification is not required. But a serious commitment to the craft needs to be demonstrated through published work or its equivalent. Early \u00a0and mid career writers are encouraged to apply. What to include Applications must include: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Covering letter including short biography. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Curriculum vitae. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Details of published work & any writing awards. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0A 500-word outline of work contemplated. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Samples of work (500 words maximum). PDF or Word files are preferred. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Two referee reports, from referees well placed to comment on your writing experience (view the template HERE ). How to apply Applications quoting reference number 2601264 will close on Sunday, 18 October 2026. Please find links below for Conditions of Award and further information about the Residency. Additional Information Contact: Arts Fellowship Administrator Position details: Conditions of Award Guidelines for Academic Positions: Guidelines Further Information: Department Website Create an email with a link to this vacancy: Create email Location: About Dunedin Primary Location NZL-SI-Dunedin Employment Status Fixed Term Salary Level and Range Please see information above Organisation Humanities Divisional Office Job Function Fellowships ^ Top of page | Accessibility | Copyright & Disclaimer | Contact Us | Feedback | Top of page \u00a9 Human Resources 1st Floor Registry Building PO Box 56 Dunedin 9054 New Zealand Tel 64 3 479 8269 Fax 64 3 479 8279 Email human.resources@otago.ac.nz"}, "https://otago.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=2601283": {"title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (P\u016bkeka/P\u016bkeka Matua) in Sports Development and Management", "description": "Job Description -  Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (P\u016bkeka/P\u016bkeka Matua) in Sports Development and Management (2601283) Go to the main content section. Human Resources Information for Staff Working @ Otago Join Otago About Otago University Application toolkit Living & working in New Zealand Career development & training Health & Safety HR toolkit HR policies Contacts & enquiries Current Vacancies Otago staff should use the internal version Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Jobs | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Job Page Basic Search | Advanced Search | Jobs Matching My Profile | All Jobs Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description -  Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (P\u016bkeka/P\u016bkeka Matua) in Sports Development and Management (2601283) Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (P\u016bkeka/P\u016bkeka Matua) in Sports Development and Management - 2601283 __________ SCHOOL OF PHYSICAL EDUCATION, SPORT AND EXERCISE SCIENCES TE KURA PARA-WHAKAWAI Who we are / Ko wai m\u0101tou The School of Physical Education, Sport and Exercise Sciences/Te Kura Para-Whakawai at the University of Otago/\u014ct\u0101kou Whakaihu Waka is internationally recognised for excellence in research, teaching and community engagement. Since 2017, it has been ranked among the world's top 25 universities for sport-related subjects in the QS World University Rankings. The School is home to an interdisciplinary community of scholars working across the natural sciences, social sciences, health sciences and humanities. We are committed to research that is internationally recognised, locally relevant, and responsive to the aspirations of Aotearoa New Zealand. The Role / Te Mahi We invite applications for a full-time, permanent Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Sport Development and Management. The successful applicant will have expertise in Sport Development and Management informed by critical socio-cultural, policy and management scholarship. Key responsibilities include: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Developing an impactful research programme, publishing in high-quality peer-reviewed journals, securing external research funding, and supervising postgraduate research students. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Coordinating and delivering research-informed teaching across undergraduate and postgraduate programmes, including Sport Development and Management (SPEX209), Advanced Sport Management (SPEX314), and Advanced Topics in Sport Management and Policy (SPEX461) with contributions to the taught Master of Sport Development and Management. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Contributing to curriculum development and academic leadership within the Sport Development and Management major. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Contributing to the effective operation of the School through service, engagement and collegial participation within the University and wider community. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Promoting and contributing to the University's commitment to Te Tiriti o Waitangi and its M\u0101ori and Pacific strategic frameworks. Your skills and experience / K\u0101 p\u016bkeka me k\u0101 wheako To be successful in this role candidates will have: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0A completed doctoral degree in Sport Development, Sport Management, Sport Leadership, or a closely related field. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Experience of effective undergraduate and postgraduate teaching in a tertiary environment. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0A strong publication record, commensurate with career stage, and demonstrated potential to secure competitive research funding. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Experience supervising postgraduate research students. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Commitment to upholding values, tikanga, kawa and traditions as guided by Ng\u0101i Tahu, mana whenua in the region. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Ability to build productive collaborations and work collegially. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Practical experience supporting sport development and management initiatives within communities, including indigenous contexts, is desirable. Further Details / P\u016broko This is a unique opportunity for an energetic, creative and committed academic to make a significant contribution to Sport Development and Management through teaching, research and engagement while joining a collegial and dynamic School. Sport Development and Management is a vibrant area within the School, with strengths in policy, management, sociology, coaching, psychology and history. The School values collaboration, equity and inclusion and is committed to Te Tiriti o Waitangi and the University's M\u0101ori, Pacific and Sustainability Strategic Frameworks. Applicants should be familiar with the University's strategic direction through Pae Tata: Strategic Plan to 2030. This is a permanent, full-time (1 FTE) position based in \u014ctepoti, Dunedin. The appointment range for a Lecturer is $97,377 to $114,943 and Senior Lecturer is $120,494 to $137,444. Specific enquiries may be directed to Professor Michael Sam, Interim Dean, School of Physical Education, Sport and Exercise Sciences via the contact details below. Application/Tono Candidates are requested to submit: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0A CV. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0A letter of application \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a03-4 Referee contact details, including telephone number and email address To submit your application please click the apply button below. Applications quoting reference number 2601283 will close on Sunday,18 October 2026. Additional Information Contact: Professor Michael Sam Position details: Information Statement Guidelines for Academic Positions: Guidelines Further Information: Department Website Create an email with a link to this vacancy: Create email Location: About Dunedin Primary Location NZL-SI-Dunedin Employment Status Permanent Salary Level and Range Lecturer / Research Fellow ($97,377 to $114,943) or Senior Lecturer / Senior Research Fellow ($120,494 to $137,444) Organisation School of Physical Education, Sport and Exercise Sciences Job Function Teaching ^ Top of page | Accessibility | Copyright & Disclaimer | Contact Us | Feedback | Top of page \u00a9 Human Resources 1st Floor Registry Building PO Box 56 Dunedin 9054 New Zealand Tel 64 3 479 8269 Fax 64 3 479 8279 Email human.resources@otago.ac.nz"}, "https://otago.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=2601461": {"title": "Senior HR Adviser (Christchurch)", "description": "Job Description - Senior HR Adviser (Christchurch) (2601461) Go to the main content section. Human Resources Information for Staff Working @ Otago Join Otago About Otago University Application toolkit Living & working in New Zealand Career development & training Health & Safety HR toolkit HR policies Contacts & enquiries Current Vacancies Otago staff should use the internal version Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Jobs | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Job Page Basic Search | Advanced Search | Jobs Matching My Profile | All Jobs Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Senior HR Adviser (Christchurch) (2601461) Senior HR Adviser (Christchurch) - 2601461 __________ HUMAN RESOURCES DIVISION | TE W\u0100HANGA MATUA P\u016aMANAWA TANGATA UNIVERSITY OF OTAGO | \u014cT\u0100KOU WHAKAIHU WAKA \u014ct\u0101kou Whakaihu Waka The University of Otago | \u014ct\u0101kou Whakaihu Waka has been a renowned place of learning and discovery for more than 150 years. We strive to become an even more successful, globally influential university, committed to upholding the principles of Te Tiriti o Waitangi as we advance outstanding research and research-informed teaching to enable transformative learning and student experiences. Our Vision/Ko te Aronga is for our people and knowledge to transform lives, connect communities and nurture the environment in \u014ct\u0101kou, Te Waipounamu, Aotearoa, the Pacific, and the world. This is a rare opportunity to be part of a collaborative and dedicated HR team. We are looking for an experienced and confident HR generalist, who enjoys working independently to develop pragmatic HR solutions for clients, to join us. The role | Te mahi Working closely with the Divisional HR Manager and the Dean/Head of Region \u2013 Faculty of Medicine Christchurch, you will provide senior generalist HR advice and support to clients on our Christchurch Campus. This will involve the provision of HR technical guidance and support on a range of issues including disputes resolution, personal grievances, management of conduct and capability, change management, training and development, recruitment and selection, health and safety support and effective implementation of HR policies, procedures and best practice. You will have the support of a comprehensive HR infrastructure, and colleagues both within the HR Advisory team and across the wider Human Resources Division. Your skills and experience | K\u0101 p\u016bkeka me k\u0101 wheako We are looking for a professional who will champion our values: Manaakitaka/Respect, Pono/Integrity, M\u0101hirahira/Curiosity and Wharawhanaukataka/Community. You will also have: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0A tertiary qualification in a relevant field. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Well-developed understanding of HR processes and policies. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Recent experience in a generalist HR role. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Excellent knowledge of NZ employment legislation and its application. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Confidence with technology, including the ability to quickly learn and adapt to new digital tools and systems. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Dedication to working in a culturally safe and respectful manner, including understanding and appreciation of Te Ao M\u0101ori, Te Tiriti o Waitangi principles, and Pasifika values. You will be effective communicator and facilitator, with proven success in building effective professional relationships. Further details | P\u016broko This is a permanent, part-time (28 hours per week) position based in \u014ctautahi, Christchurch. The University of Otago, Christchurch is the base for undergraduate medical and postgraduate health education and health research in Christchurch. We collaborate closely in our research and student programmes with the region\u2019s hospitals run by Health New Zealand | Te Whatu Ora, and other community health agencies. The appointment salary range for this role is $101,739 to $110,396 per annum (pro-rata). Top of range is $119,053. You must have the right to live and work in New Zealand to apply for this position. For further information or to discuss the role in confidence - please contact Simone McNichol, Divisional HR Manager via the contact details below. Application | Tono To submit your application (including CV and cover letter) please click the apply button. Applications quoting reference number 2601461 will close on Sunday, 18 October 2026. Additional Information Note: As a part-time position, the salary range for this role will be the pro-rata equivalent of the annual full-time salary range listed. Contact: Simone McNichol Position details: Job Description Further Information: Department Website Create an email with a link to this vacancy: Create email Location: About Christchurch Primary Location NZL-SI-Christchurch Employment Status Permanent Salary Level and Range Management Band 2 (Range of Appointments $101,739 to $110,396, Top of Range $119,053) Organisation Human Resources Divisional Office Job Function HR Adviser ^ Top of page | Accessibility | Copyright & Disclaimer | Contact Us | Feedback | Top of page \u00a9 Human Resources 1st Floor Registry Building PO Box 56 Dunedin 9054 New Zealand Tel 64 3 479 8269 Fax 64 3 479 8279 Email human.resources@otago.ac.nz"}, "https://otago.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=2601356": {"title": "Project Manager", "description": "Job Description - Project Manager - Centre for International Health (2601356) Go to the main content section. Human Resources Information for Staff Working @ Otago Join Otago About Otago University Application toolkit Living & working in New Zealand Career development & training Health & Safety HR toolkit HR policies Contacts & enquiries Current Vacancies Otago staff should use the internal version Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Jobs | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Job Page Basic Search | Advanced Search | Jobs Matching My Profile | All Jobs Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Project Manager - Centre for International Health (2601356) Project Manager - Centre for International Health - 2601356 __________ CENTRE FOR INTERNATIONAL HEALTH | TE POKAP\u016a RANGAHAU HAUORA O TE AO DIVISION OF HEALTH SCIENCES | TE TAUTARINUI About the Centre | M\u014d te t\u012bma The Centre for International Health is a vibrant hub for global health research, education, and collaboration within the University of Otago's Division of Health Sciences. As a key part of the Otago Global Health Institute (OGHI), a University Research Centre bringing together more than 170 researchers across disciplines, we foster innovative partnerships that address complex health challenges around the world. Working closely with collaborators in resource-limited settings, we advance research that improves health outcomes and strengthens health systems globally. Alongside our research mission, we are committed to developing the next generation of global health leaders through high-quality postgraduate training, strategic mentorship, and meaningful international engagement. The role | Te mahi We are seeking a highly organised and collaborative Project Manager to oversee the administration and delivery of a major international, multi-centre observational study within the Centre for International Health. The study is generating critical evidence to inform future Phase III vaccine trials for invasive nontyphoidal Salmonella disease, a major cause of severe illness and mortality among children in Africa. Working closely with researchers, funders, and international collaborators, you will lead all aspects of project management, including communications, stakeholder engagement, reporting and regulatory compliance, financial oversight, and the coordination of study activities. This is an excellent opportunity to contribute to impactful global health research while working in a collaborative, multidisciplinary environment. You will join a team committed to research excellence, strong international partnerships, and improving health outcomes in resource-limited settings. Skills and experience | K\u0101 p\u016bkeka me k\u0101 wheako The successful candidate will be a highly motivated and adaptable individual who enjoys working both independently and collaboratively with global research partners. You will have strong project management capability, and a meticulous approach to organising information and maintaining accurate records. You will be comfortable working with complex research data, managing competing priorities, and building effective relationships across diverse international teams. To be successful in this role, you will have: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Relevant qualifications in project management or a related field. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Experience managing large research projects or studies. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Excellent interpersonal skills. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Outstanding written and verbal communication skills in English. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0The ability to quickly learn new skills and adapt to changing requirements. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Strong problem-solving and critical-thinking skills. Further details | P\u016broko This is a part-time (0.5 FTE), fixed term position for 30 months, located in \u014ctepoti, Dunedin. The University is offering a remuneration level commensurate with the responsibilities of the position The University of Otago is a workplace that values and utilises diverse and inclusive thinking, people, and behaviours. This means that the contributions of staff with diverse backgrounds, experiences, skills, and perspectives are valued and respected. Specific enquiries about the position may be directed to Professor John A. Crump, Centre for International Health via the contact details below. Application | Tono To submit your application (including CV and cover letter) please click the apply button. Applications quoting reference number 2601356 will close on Sunday, 25 October 2026. Applications may be considered as they are received. The University reserves the right to close this vacancy at any time. Additional Information Note: As a part-time position, the salary range for this role will be the pro-rata equivalent of the annual full-time salary range listed. Contact: Professor John A. Crump Tel: +64 3 479 9460 Position details: Job Description Further Information: Department Website Create an email with a link to this vacancy: Create email Location: About Dunedin Primary Location NZL-SI-Dunedin Employment Status Fixed Term Salary Level and Range The University is offering a remuneration level commensurate with the responsibilities of the position. Organisation Centre for International Health Job Function Research ^ Top of page | Accessibility | Copyright & Disclaimer | Contact Us | Feedback | Top of page \u00a9 Human Resources 1st Floor Registry Building PO Box 56 Dunedin 9054 New Zealand Tel 64 3 479 8269 Fax 64 3 479 8279 Email human.resources@otago.ac.nz"}, "https://otago.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=2601500": {"title": "Warden", "description": "Job Description - Warden | Tautiaki - Cumberland College (2601500) Go to the main content section. Human Resources Information for Staff Working @ Otago Join Otago About Otago University Application toolkit Living & working in New Zealand Career development & training Health & Safety HR toolkit HR policies Contacts & enquiries Current Vacancies Otago staff should use the internal version Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Jobs | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Job Page Basic Search | Advanced Search | Jobs Matching My Profile | All Jobs Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Warden | Tautiaki - Cumberland College (2601500) Warden | Tautiaki - Cumberland College - 2601500 __________ CAMPUS AND COLLEGIATE LIFE SERVICES | TE URU KAHIKA CUMBERLAND COLLEGE | TE K\u0100RETI O CUMBERLAND The University of Otago is renowned for its vibrant residential college communities, which support thousands of predominantly first-year students as they transition into university life. Established in 1989, Te K\u0101reti o Cumberland is home to 325 residents. The Tautiaki plays a pivotal role in extending manaakitanga to all members of the college community. At the heart of our kaupapa is fostering a strong sense of whanaungatanga, creating a supportive environment that underpins both the academic success and personal development of Cumberland tauira. The role | Te mahi The Tautiaki of Te K\u0101reti o Cumberland is a leadership role responsible for the effective and efficient provision of a collegiate experience for its tauira/residents and wider associated community. The primary role is to support our residents to reach their highest academic potential, while also providing opportunities for residents to experience cultural, sporting and personal development. We seek an experienced senior leader with proven success in dealing with the demands of a multi-faceted operation - managing people and communities. Your skills and experience | K\u0101 p\u016bkeka me k\u0101 wheako Our ideal candidate will: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0be professionally and personally resilient and capable of handling (sometimes) difficult and complex situations, \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0have demonstrated leadership, management and organisation skills, \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0have the ability to perform effectively and professionally in a complex and challenging environment, including mental health and resident wellbeing related incidents, \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0have experience of operating a significant budget and associated administration, \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0develop effective sundry income streams including meeting rooms, hospitality, conferences, etc., \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0assist in the wider division in projects and support, \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0have the ability to influence and negotiate in a practical way, and \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0be trusted to act in a calm manner. A minimum of a degree-level tertiary qualification is essential and experience in the tertiary sector would be a distinct advantage. Further details | P\u016broko This is a full-time permanent live-in position and as such you will be required to reside in accommodation, which is provided by the University. \u00a0The remuneration package includes on-call duties. \u00a0An allowance will be paid to offset the cost of accommodation. The appointment range for this role is $107,320 to $115,834. Top of range $124,348 per annum. The University is committed to meeting its obligations under the Vulnerable Children Act 2014. Candidates who successfully make the final stages of the recruitment process will be required to undergo a police safety check. Confidential enquiries can be directed to Dr Sean McCallaghan, Senior Warden of Colleges, Campus and Collegiate Life Services Division. Application | Tono To submit your application (including CV and cover letter) please click the apply button below. Applications quoting reference number 2601500 will close on Sunday, 25 October. Applications may be reviewed as they are received. The University reserves the right to close this vacancy at any time. Additional Information Contact: Dr Sean McCallaghan Tel: 021 2791130 Position details: Job Description Further Information: Department Website Create an email with a link to this vacancy: Create email Location: About Dunedin Primary Location NZL-SI-Dunedin Employment Status Permanent Salary Level and Range Management Band 3 (Range of Appointments $107,320 to $115,834, Top of Range $124,348) Organisation Cumberland College Job Function Administrative and Operations Management ^ Top of page | Accessibility | Copyright & Disclaimer | Contact Us | Feedback | Top of page \u00a9 Human Resources 1st Floor Registry Building PO Box 56 Dunedin 9054 New Zealand Tel 64 3 479 8269 Fax 64 3 479 8279 Email human.resources@otago.ac.nz"}, "https://otago.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=2601483": {"title": "Administrator", "description": "Job Description - Administrator - Student Administration (2601483) Go to the main content section. Human Resources Information for Staff Working @ Otago Join Otago About Otago University Application toolkit Living & working in New Zealand Career development & training Health & Safety HR toolkit HR policies Contacts & enquiries Current Vacancies Otago staff should use the internal version Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Jobs | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Job Page Basic Search | Advanced Search | Jobs Matching My Profile | All Jobs Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Administrator - Student Administration (2601483) Administrator - Student Administration - 2601483 __________ ACADEMIC DIVISION | TE W\u0100HAKA MATUA M\u0100TAURAKA STUDENT EXPERIENCE Your new adventure starts here! Join the team responsible for supporting University of Otago students who represent our future New Zealand thinkers. We work to smooth the Otago journey for 21,000 students, receiving and validating applications, maintaining student records, managing the examination process, and each year supporting thousands of bright minds as they graduate from the University of Otago. We are the Student Administration team within the Academic Division. About the role | Te mahi Your tasks within the Student Administration team will depend on the specific portfolio you are supporting; this role is based predominantly in the course management team. \u00a0A full list of tasks and responsibilities can be found within the job description. Due to the nature of the role, the range of tasks and responsibilities is broad and may require performing duties at different workplaces or locations across campus. We are committed to on-going training and development in order to upskill successful candidates in areas that they desire more exposure to. Your Skills and Experience | K\u0101 p\u016bkeka me k\u0101 wheako We are looking for candidates with: \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Exposure to work in a busy administration environment. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Outstanding attention to detail and accuracy. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0A passion for customer service and delivering exceptional service to students and staff. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0An ability to work independently but also collaboratively within a team environment. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Strong Microsoft office and PC skills. Who we are | M\u014d te t\u012bma Our team of professional staff focus on the experience felt by our students here at the University of Otago. Our wider Academic Division is responsible for strategic oversight of teaching and learning policy and practice, oversight of academic staff confirmation and promotion, and other various teams which provide support to our student community. Further Details | P\u016broko This is a permanent, full-time (37.5 hours) position, located in Dunedin. The appointment salary range for this role is $63,508 to $68,185 per annum. Top of range is $73,640. You must have the right to live and work in New Zealand to apply for this job. For further information, please contact Khazima Tahir, Lead Administrator Student Administration via the contact details below. Application | Tono To submit your application please click the apply button. Applications quoting reference number 2601483 will close on Thursday, 22 October 2026. Applications may be reviewed as they are received. The University reserves the right to close this vacancy at any time. Additional Information Contact: Khazima Tahir Position details: Job Description Further Information: Department Website Create an email with a link to this vacancy: Create email Location: About Dunedin Primary Location NZL-SI-Dunedin Employment Status Permanent Salary Level and Range Level 4 (Range of Appointments $63,508 to $68,185, Top of Range $73,640) Organisation Student Experience Job Function Administrative ^ Top of page | Accessibility | Copyright & Disclaimer | Contact Us | Feedback | Top of page \u00a9 Human Resources 1st Floor Registry Building PO Box 56 Dunedin 9054 New Zealand Tel 64 3 479 8269 Fax 64 3 479 8279 Email human.resources@otago.ac.nz"}, "https://otago.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=2601357": {"title": "Administrator (Wellington)", "description": "Job Description - Administrator (Wellington) (2601357) Go to the main content section. Human Resources Information for Staff Working @ Otago Join Otago About Otago University Application toolkit Living & working in New Zealand Career development & training Health & Safety HR toolkit HR policies Contacts & enquiries Current Vacancies Otago staff should use the internal version Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Jobs | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Job Page Basic Search | Advanced Search | Jobs Matching My Profile | All Jobs Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Administrator (Wellington) (2601357) Administrator (Wellington) - 2601357 __________ DIVISIONAL SERVICES & ADMINISTRATION | WHAKARATONGA TARI ME TE WHAKARITENGA UNIVERSITY OF OTAGO, WELLINGTON | \u014cT\u0100KOU WHAKAIHU WAKA, P\u014cNEKE Who we are/M\u014d te t\u012bma At the University of Otago Wellington campus, we teach medicine, radiation therapy, physiotherapy, and a wide range of postgraduate qualifications and papers, while undertaking a diverse portfolio of health-based research. We are proud to be a part of New Zealand's first medical school and have been providing New Zealand with a highly qualified health professional workforce since 1875. Our campus is supported by a team of highly skilled professional staff, working collaboratively to deliver an outstanding student and staff experience. This is achieved through the provision of high-quality administrative and operational support to our students, academic staff, researchers, and external stakeholders. About the role/Te mahi Are you an exceptional administrator who wants to play a vital role in the education of New Zealand's future health professionals and support some of New Zealand's leading health researchers? If so, this could be the opportunity for you. In these Administrator roles, you will provide proactive administrative, teaching, and timetabling support across a range of undergraduate and postgraduate programmes. You will become a trusted point of contact for students, academic staff, researchers, and visitors while contributing to the successful delivery of teaching and research activities across the Wellington campus. Key responsibilities may include: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Providing high-quality administrative support, including document preparation, minute taking, records management, and correspondence. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Coordinating student rosters across academic and clinical learning environments. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Supporting teaching activities, timetabling, clinical placements, and programme administration for undergraduate and postgraduate programmes. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Coordinating student assessments and examination-related processes. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Maintaining databases and records within University systems, producing reports and extracting relevant data as required. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Providing administrative coordination and support to academic staff, researchers, and programme leaders. Alongside excellent administrative and organisational abilities, a strong customer service focus and the ability to build positive working relationships are critical to success in this role. Your skills and experience/K\u0101 p\u016bkeka me k\u0101 wheako We are looking for candidates who have: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Proven experience in a busy administrative or coordination role. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0A passion for delivering exceptional service and support to customers and stakeholders. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Proficiency in the Microsoft Office suite and confidence working with a range of systems and databases. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work collaboratively as part of a team. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Strong organisational skills, attention to detail, and a willingness to learn. If you have outstanding organisational and administration skills and want to contribute to the successful delivery of undergraduate and postgraduate health professional education programmes, we'd love to hear from you. Further details/P\u016broko This is a full-time (37.5 hours per week) position, based in Wellington. You must have the right to live and work in New Zealand to apply for this job. The salary range for an Administrator is Level 4 ($63,508\u2013$73,640). Candidates with M\u0101ori competency may also be considered for the Kaiwhakahaere Tari (Level 5) pathway, and candidates with Pacific cultural competency may be considered for the Administrator - Pacific Peoples (Level 5) pathway. Both Level 5 roles support the University\u2019s M\u0101ori and Pacific Strategic Frameworks by applying M\u0101ori and Pacific values and perspectives to administrative practice and supporting student and staff success. Salary range for Level 5 roles is $69,931\u2013$80,285. The University of Otago is a workplace that values and utilises diverse and inclusive thinking, people, and behaviours. This means that the contributions of staff with diverse backgrounds, experiences, skills, and perspectives are valued and respected. For further information, please contact Shan Valiyara via the contact details below. Application/Tono To submit your application (including CV and cover letter) please click the apply button below. Applications quoting reference number 2601357 will close Sunday, 18 October 2026. Applications will be reviewed as submitted and candidates may be invited to interview immediately. The University reserves the right to close this vacancy at any time. #LI-DNI Additional Information Contact: Shan Valiyara Position details: Administrator - Job Description Position details: Kaiwhakahaere Tari - Job Description Position details: Pacific Peoples - Job Description Further Information: Department Website Create an email with a link to this vacancy: Create email Location: About Wellington Primary Location NZL-NI-Wellington Employment Status Permanent Salary Level and Range Please see information above Organisation Divisional Services and Administration (UOW) Job Function Administrative ^ Top of page | Accessibility | Copyright & Disclaimer | Contact Us | Feedback | Top of page \u00a9 Human Resources 1st Floor Registry Building PO Box 56 Dunedin 9054 New Zealand Tel 64 3 479 8269 Fax 64 3 479 8279 Email human.resources@otago.ac.nz"}, "https://otago.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=2601411": {"title": "Research Technician", "description": "Job Description - Research Technician - Surgery and Critical Care (2601411) Go to the main content section. Human Resources Information for Staff Working @ Otago Join Otago About Otago University Application toolkit Living & working in New Zealand Career development & training Health & Safety HR toolkit HR policies Contacts & enquiries Current Vacancies Otago staff should use the internal version Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Jobs | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Job Page Basic Search | Advanced Search | Jobs Matching My Profile | All Jobs Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Technician - Surgery and Critical Care (2601411) Research Technician - Surgery and Critical Care - 2601411 __________ DEPARTMENT OF SURGERY AND CRITICAL CARE, DUNEDIN | TE TARI H\u0100PARAPARA, TE TARI WH\u0100OMOOMO DUNEDIN SCHOOL OF MEDICINE | TE KURA WHAIORA A \u014cTEPOTI \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Are you interested in the outcomes of exercise on postoperative care? \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Do you like working independently as part of a larger group? \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Do you have great interpersonal and organisational skills? \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Are you looking for part-time, flexible work? About our team/M\u014d te t\u012bma The Department of Surgical Sciences excels in clinical teaching and training, linking science with clinical research, and developing our discipline nationally and internationally. Our dynamic research group, based in Dunedin Hospital, is conducting a range of innovative clinical research projects focused on improving surgical outcomes. The role/Te mahi We are seeking a motivated and detail-oriented Research Technician to support several ongoing studies. This is an exciting opportunity to work across diverse clinical areas and contribute to meaningful improvements in patient care. Key responsibilities include: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Training and testing for a HIIT-based project aimed at improving postoperative outcomes. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Recruit patients; schedule interviews and assist with data collection. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Sign up participants, collect clinical data, and take rectal swabs for a colorectal surgery study. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Enlist patients, collect urine samples, and coordinate with the K9MD team. Your skills and experience/K\u0101 p\u016bkeka me k\u0101 wheako You will have some understanding of health issues, gained through relevant study or experience (e.g. as a medical, physiotherapy, or nursing student, or as a health assistant). Key will be your excellent organisational and interpersonal skills, including the ability to build rapport with patients and interact with compassion and tact. You will be able to work independently and have initiative in problem solving. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Hold a current first aid certificate. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Strong organisation and time management skills with meticulous record-keeping. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Proficiency in common computer applications. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Excellent communication skills, the ability to work both independently and as part of a team. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Adaptability to changing research needs. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Flexibility to work outside core hours when required. Further details/P\u016broko This is a fixed-term, variable-hours position (with a guaranteed minimum of 15 hours per week) based in Dunedin, ending on 30 June 2027. Actual hours may vary depending on participant availability and project needs and will be scheduled in consultation with the successful candidate. There is scope for hours to exceed the minimum hours with the possibility of the maximum number of hours over the term of the contract being up to 30 hours a week. The appointment range for this role is $63,508 to $68,185 Top of Range $73,640 (pro rata). You must have the right to live and work in New Zealand to apply for this position. The University of Otago is a workplace that values and utilises diverse and inclusive thinking, people, and behaviours. This means that the contributions of staff with diverse backgrounds, experiences, skills, and perspectives are valued and respected. Specific inquiries regarding the role can be directed to Dr Kari Clifford, Department of Surgical Sciences, via the contact details below. Application/Tono To submit your application (including CV and cover letter) please click the apply button. Applications quoting reference number 2601411 will close on Wednesday, 21 October 2026. Applications will be reviewed as submitted and candidates may be invited to interview immediately. The University reserves the right to close this vacancy at any time. Additional Information Contact: Dr Kari Clifford Position details: Job Description Further Information: Department Website Create an email with a link to this vacancy: Create email Location: About Dunedin Primary Location NZL-SI-Dunedin Employment Status Fixed Term Salary Level and Range Level 4 (Range of Appointments $63,508 to $68,185, Top of Range $73,640) Organisation Surgery and Critical Care Job Function Medical and Science Technicians ^ Top of page | Accessibility | Copyright & Disclaimer | Contact Us | Feedback | Top of page \u00a9 Human Resources 1st Floor Registry Building PO Box 56 Dunedin 9054 New Zealand Tel 64 3 479 8269 Fax 64 3 479 8279 Email human.resources@otago.ac.nz"}, "https://otago.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=2601492": {"title": "Professional Practice Fellow / Senior Professional Practice Fellow", "description": "Job Description - Professional Practice Fellow / Senior Professional Practice Fellow - Classical Voice (2601492) Go to the main content section. Human Resources Information for Staff Working @ Otago Join Otago About Otago University Application toolkit Living & working in New Zealand Career development & training Health & Safety HR toolkit HR policies Contacts & enquiries Current Vacancies Otago staff should use the internal version Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Jobs | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Job Page Basic Search | Advanced Search | Jobs Matching My Profile | All Jobs Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professional Practice Fellow / Senior Professional Practice Fellow - Classical Voice (2601492) Professional Practice Fellow / Senior Professional Practice Fellow - Classical Voice - 2601492 __________ SCHOOL OF PERFORMING ARTS | TE K\u0100HUI TAU DIVISION OF HUMANITIES | TE KETE ARONUI About our team/M\u014d te t\u012bma At the creative heart of the University, the School of Performing Arts is a vibrant and inclusive community where music takes centre stage. Our students and staff are passionate performers, composers, songwriters, educators and researchers, combining professional practice with innovative teaching and scholarship. Through our music programme, students develop their artistic voice, creative problem-solving abilities, collaborative skills and discipline-specific expertise, while gaining the confidence to express themselves and connect with audiences. Committed to excellence, we foster a supportive and respectful environment that inspires creativity, nurtures talent, and cultivates a lifelong passion for music and the performing arts. The role/Te mahi The School of Performing Arts is seeking an accomplished and passionate Classical Voice educator and performer to join our Music Programme. This is an exciting opportunity to inspire aspiring singers through high-quality individual and group teaching while contributing to a thriving artistic and academic community. As a Professional Practice Fellow or Senior Professional Practice Fellow, you will provide specialist tuition in classical voice, supporting students to develop the technical, artistic and professional skills needed for successful performance careers. Working with undergraduate and postgraduate students, you will participate in audition and assessment processes, contribute to student recruitment activities, and play an active role in performances and wider School initiatives. You will also maintain your own professional practice, ensuring your teaching remains current and informed by contemporary developments in the field. As a valued member of the Music Programme, you will contribute to a collaborative and supportive environment that promotes excellence in performance and student success. Skills and experience/K\u0101 p\u016bkeka me k\u0101 wheako We are looking for a recognised Classical Voice practitioner with a strong commitment to teaching and mentoring emerging performers. You will bring a combination of professional performance experience, outstanding teaching capability, and the ability to engage effectively with a diverse range of students and stakeholders. To be successful in this role, you will have: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0An established professional career in classical vocal performance. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Demonstrated excellence in one-to-one and group vocal teaching. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Strong communication, interpersonal and relationship-building skills. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0A commitment to creating an inclusive and supportive learning environment. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Cultural competence and an understanding of Te Tiriti o Waitangi principles and culturally safe practice. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Registration, or eligibility to register, with an appropriate professional body such as MENZA or NEWZATS. Experience teaching at tertiary level and/or directing choirs or vocal ensembles would be advantageous. Further details/P\u016broko The position is a permanent, variable hour\u2019s role based in \u014ctepoti, Dunedin. The hours allocated each year will depend on the number of students enrolled and their needs, which may result in appointing multiple Professional Practice Fellows. The appointment ranges for this role are Teaching & Professional Practice Fellow 1-2-3-4 - $75,727 to $137,444 (pro-rata). Appointment level will be determined by the candidate\u2019s academic achievements, skills, and experience and salary prorated for hours of work. You must be eligible to work in New Zealand to apply for this position. The University of Otago is a workplace that values and utilises diverse and inclusive thinking, people and behaviours. This means that the contributions of staff with diverse backgrounds, experiences, skills and perspectives are valued and respected. For further information, or to discuss the role in confidence, please contact Jennifer Cattemole, Head of School, Performing Arts via the contact details below. Application/Tono To submit your application (including CV and cover letter) please click the apply button. Applications quoting reference number 2601492 will close on Sunday, 1 November 2026. Applications will be reviewed as they are received. The University reserves the right to close this vacancy at any time. Additional Information Note: As a variable hours position, the salary range for this role will be the pro-rata equivalent of the annual full-time salary range listed. Contact: Jennifer Cattemole Tel: +64 3 479 4025 Position details: Professional Practice Fellow JD Position details: Senior Professional Practice Fellow JD Guidelines for Academic Positions: Guidelines Further Information: Department Website Create an email with a link to this vacancy: Create email Location: About Dunedin Primary Location NZL-SI-Dunedin Employment Status Permanent Salary Level and Range Teaching & Professional Practice Fellow 1 ($75,727 to $87,849) or 2 ($91,614 to $102,900) or 3 ($105,665 to $114,943) or 4 ($120,495 to $137,444) Organisation Music Job Function Teaching ^ Top of page | Accessibility | Copyright & Disclaimer | Contact Us | Feedback | Top of page \u00a9 Human Resources 1st Floor Registry Building PO Box 56 Dunedin 9054 New Zealand Tel 64 3 479 8269 Fax 64 3 479 8279 Email human.resources@otago.ac.nz"}, "https://otago.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=2601494": {"title": "Professional Practice Fellow / Senior Professional Practice Fellow", "description": "Job Description - Professional Practice Fellow / Senior Professional Practice Fellow - Contemporary and Musical Theatre Voice (2601494) Go to the main content section. Human Resources Information for Staff Working @ Otago Join Otago About Otago University Application toolkit Living & working in New Zealand Career development & training Health & Safety HR toolkit HR policies Contacts & enquiries Current Vacancies Otago staff should use the internal version Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Jobs | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Job Page Basic Search | Advanced Search | Jobs Matching My Profile | All Jobs Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professional Practice Fellow / Senior Professional Practice Fellow - Contemporary and Musical Theatre Voice (2601494) Professional Practice Fellow / Senior Professional Practice Fellow - Contemporary and Musical Theatre Voice - 2601494 __________ SCHOOL OF PERFORMING ARTS | TE K\u0100HUI TAU DIVISION OF HUMANITIES | TE KETE ARONUI About our team/M\u014d te t\u012bma At the creative heart of the University, the School of Performing Arts is a vibrant and inclusive community where music takes centre stage. Our students and staff are passionate performers, composers, songwriters, educators and researchers, combining professional practice with innovative teaching and scholarship. Through our music programmes, students develop their artistic voice, creative problem-solving abilities, collaborative skills and discipline-specific expertise, while gaining the confidence to express themselves and connect with audiences. Committed to excellence, we foster a supportive and respectful environment that inspires creativity, nurtures talent and cultivates a lifelong passion for music and the performing arts. The role/Te mahi As a Professional Practice Fellow or Senior Professional Practice Fellow, you will provide specialist teaching across contemporary commercial music and musical theatre vocal styles. You will deliver engaging individual and group tuition, support auditions and assessments, and contribute to a dynamic learning environment that prepares students for diverse performance careers. Working closely with colleagues and students, you will help shape a vibrant performance culture through participation in productions, showcases, recruitment activities, and broader School initiatives. You will also maintain an active professional practice, ensuring students benefit from current industry knowledge and contemporary vocal pedagogy. Skills and experience/K\u0101 p\u016bkeka me k\u0101 wheako You will be an accomplished performer and educator with expertise in contemporary and/or musical theatre voice. Passionate about developing emerging artists, you will have the skills to support students in building technical mastery, performance confidence, stylistic versatility, and industry readiness. To be successful in this role, you will have: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0An established professional background in contemporary music and/or musical theatre performance. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Demonstrated experience teaching voice in one-to-one and group settings. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Strong knowledge of contemporary vocal techniques and performance practice. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Excellent communication, mentoring, and stakeholder engagement skills. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0A commitment to inclusive teaching practices and student success. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Cultural competence and an understanding of Te Tiriti o Waitangi principles and culturally safe practice. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Registration, or eligibility to register, with an appropriate professional body such as MENZA or NEWSATS. Experience teaching in a tertiary setting, directing vocal ensembles, or professional experience within the musical theatre industry will be highly regarded. Further details/P\u016broko The position is a variable hours, fixed-term role for 3 years, based in \u014ctepoti, Dunedin. The hours allocated each year will depend on the number of students enrolled and their needs, which may result in appointing multiple Professional Practice Fellows. The appointment ranges for this role are Teaching & Professional Practice Fellow 1-2-3-4 - $75,727 to $137,444 (pro-rata). Appointment level will be determined by the candidate\u2019s academic achievements, skills, and experience and salary prorated for hours of work. You must be eligible to work in New Zealand to apply for this position. The University of Otago is a workplace that values and utilises diverse and inclusive thinking, people, and behaviours. This means that the contributions of staff with diverse backgrounds, experiences, skills, and perspectives are valued and respected. For further information, or to discuss the role in confidence, please contact the Head of Music, Jennifer Cattemole, Head of School, Performing Arts via the contact details below. Application/Tono To submit your application (including CV and cover letter) please click the apply button. Applications quoting reference number 2601494 will close on Sunday, 1 November 2026. Applications will be reviewed as they are received, the University reserves the right to close this vacancy at any time. Additional Information Note: As a variable hours position, the salary range for this role will be the pro-rata equivalent of the annual full-time salary range listed. Contact: Jennifer Cattemole Tel: +64 3 479 4025 Position details: Professional Practice Fellow-JD Position details: Senior Professional Practice Fellow-JD Guidelines for Academic Positions: Guidelines Further Information: Department Website Create an email with a link to this vacancy: Create email Location: About Dunedin Primary Location NZL-SI-Dunedin Employment Status Fixed Term Salary Level and Range Teaching & Professional Practice Fellow 1 ($75,727 to $87,849) or 2 ($91,614 to $102,900) or 3 ($105,665 to $114,943) or 4 ($120,495 to $137,444) Organisation Music Job Function Teaching ^ Top of page | Accessibility | Copyright & Disclaimer | Contact Us | Feedback | Top of page \u00a9 Human Resources 1st Floor Registry Building PO Box 56 Dunedin 9054 New Zealand Tel 64 3 479 8269 Fax 64 3 479 8279 Email human.resources@otago.ac.nz"}, "https://otago.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=2601516": {"title": "Finance Associate", "description": "Job Description - Finance Associate (2601516) Go to the main content section. Human Resources Information for Staff Working @ Otago Join Otago About Otago University Application toolkit Living & working in New Zealand Career development & training Health & Safety HR toolkit HR policies Contacts & enquiries Current Vacancies Otago staff should use the internal version Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Jobs | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Job Page Basic Search | Advanced Search | Jobs Matching My Profile | All Jobs Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Finance Associate (2601516) Finance Associate - 2601516 __________ FINANCE ADVISORY FINANCIAL SERVICES DIVISION (FSD) | TE RATOKA P\u016aTEA Who we are | Ko wai m\u0101tou The University of Otago is New Zealand's oldest University and has a strong teaching and research tradition and well-established national and international linkages. It is also one of New Zealand's largest universities, with over 20,000 students, assets in excess of $2.0 billion and 4,000 full-time equivalent staff based in Dunedin, Christchurch, Wellington, Auckland and Invercargill. Ranked within the top 1% of universities in the world, the University of Otago recognises that our staff are the key to our success. The role | Te mahi As a Finance Associate, you will provide expert financial advice, analysis and day-to-day support to executives and managers that strengthen the business unit\u2019s finances and support effective decision making. This role is part of the central Finance Advisory team of 50 staff and reports to the Finance Manager. We have two positions available, one supporting our Health Sciences Division, and the other supporting our Humanities Division. Skills and experience | K\u0101 p\u016bkeka me k\u0101 wheako We are looking for individuals with experience in: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Providing financial advisory services, including month end accounting; financial reporting, analysis and commentary; financial forecasting and budgeting; financial modelling and analysis. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Stakeholder engagement. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Giving financial advice and guidance to non-finance senior managers. Recognised qualification(s) appropriate to the role and considerable relevant finance experience are essential for the role. A tertiary level qualification in an accounting/finance discipline is preferred. Further details | P\u016broko These are full-time (37.5 hours), permanent roles located in \u014ctepoti, Dunedin. The appointment range for this position is $75,631 to $80,503. Top of range $88,750 per annum. You must have the right to live and work in New Zealand to apply for this position. For further information, or to discuss the role in confidence \u2013 please contact Fraser Hunter (Divisional Manager Finance, Health Sciences) or Quentin Johnson (Divisional Manager Finance, Humanities) via the contact details below. Application | Tono To submit your application (including CV and cover letter) please click the apply button below. Applications quoting reference number 2601516 will close on Sunday, 1 November 2026. Additional Information Contact: Fraser Hunter - Health Sciences Contact: Quentin Johnson - Humanities Position details: Job Description Further Information: Department Website Create an email with a link to this vacancy: Create email Location: About Dunedin Primary Location NZL-SI-Dunedin Employment Status Permanent Salary Level and Range Level 6 (Range of Appointments $75,631 to $80,503, Top of Range $88,750) Organisation Finance Advisory Service Job Function Accountant and Analyst ^ Top of page | Accessibility | Copyright & Disclaimer | Contact Us | Feedback | Top of page \u00a9 Human Resources 1st Floor Registry Building PO Box 56 Dunedin 9054 New Zealand Tel 64 3 479 8269 Fax 64 3 479 8279 Email human.resources@otago.ac.nz"}, "https://otago.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=2601504": {"title": "Clinic Administrator", "description": "Job Description - Clinic Administrator - Student Health (2601504) Go to the main content section. Human Resources Information for Staff Working @ Otago Join Otago About Otago University Application toolkit Living & working in New Zealand Career development & training Health & Safety HR toolkit HR policies Contacts & enquiries Current Vacancies Otago staff should use the internal version Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Jobs | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Job Page Basic Search | Advanced Search | Jobs Matching My Profile | All Jobs Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinic Administrator - Student Health (2601504) Clinic Administrator - Student Health - 2601504 __________ STUDENT HEALTH SERVICES | TE RATOKA HAUORA \u0100KOKA Our team | M\u014d te t\u012bma Student Health Services (SHS) provide a full range of primary health care services for students at the University of Otago. We have an experienced team of 65 full and part-time staff including GPs, Nurses, Mental Health and Wellbeing, and Administration staff who provide approximately 45,000 appointments per annum. The large and diverse health team and the distinctive campus provide a stimulating and challenging multidisciplinary work environment. Student Health Services is committed to equity and diversity and seeks to provide an accessible, respectful and welcoming environment in which all students and staff receive the individual support and resources they need. SHS promotes and upholds equity in its processes, and values the individual differences that enrich its community. We are recognised as a Rainbow Tick certified employer and a Foundation certified and Cornerstone accredited practice, which means we meet a standard of inclusivity and manaakitanga for our staff and students, and we are committed to continuous improvement. The role | Te mahi As a Clinic Administrator, you will provide effective and efficient administrative support to staff, students and patients for our Student Health Services. A strong customer service focus and confidentiality are critical to success in this role. Some key tasks include: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Providing reception services. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Patient registration and updating information. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Booking appointments for students and clinicians. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Processing referrals. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Assisting clinicians with reporting. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Utilising computer systems and billing. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Undertaking external agency processes such as ACC claims registration, processing and management. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Confidential management of patient records. Your skills and experience | K\u0101 p\u016bkeka me k\u0101 wheako \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Previous experience working in a busy, complex working environment that requires a high level of discretion, sensitivity, accuracy and interpersonal interaction. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Previous experience working in the health sector and in particular, a medical practice would be highly advantageous (but not necessary) as would knowledge of patient management systems (Medtech Evolution or similar). \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Capable of managing multiple priorities with a strong sense of urgency. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Demonstrate well-developed computing skills and proven competency with a range of software applications. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Work proactively and supportively within a team to create a positive culture. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Commitment and ability to work in a multi-disciplinary team. Further details | P\u016broko This is a permanent, part-time (15 hours), semester only vacancy located in \u014ctepoti, Dunedin. Hours of work are Monday & Tuesday 12.00pm to 8:30pm. The appointment range for this role is $63,508 to $68,185 per annum. Top of the range is $73,640 (pro-rata). You must have the right to live and work in New Zealand to apply for this role. The University of Otago\u2019s aspires to be a Te Tiriti-led university that is committed to partnership with mana whenua and upholding Te Tiriti o Waitangi. The University is committed to meeting its obligations under the Childrens Act 2014. Candidates who successfully make the final stages of the recruitment process will be required to undergo a safety check. For further information or to discuss the role in confidence please contact Brylee Saunders, via the contact details below. Application | Tono To submit your application (including CV and cover letter), please click the apply button below. Applications quoting reference number 2601504 will close on Wednesday, 28 October 2026. Applications may be reviewed as they are received, and candidates may be asked to interview immediately. The University reserves the right to close this vacancy at any time. Additional Information Note: As a part-time position, the salary range for this role will be the pro-rata equivalent of the annual full-time salary range listed. Contact: Brylee Saunders Position details: Job Description Further Information: Department Website Create an email with a link to this vacancy: Create email Location: About Dunedin Primary Location NZL-SI-Dunedin Employment Status Permanent Salary Level and Range Level 4 (Range of Appointments $63,508 to $68,185, Top of Range $73,640) Organisation Student Health Services Job Function Administrative ^ Top of page | Accessibility | Copyright & Disclaimer | Contact Us | Feedback | Top of page \u00a9 Human Resources 1st Floor Registry Building PO Box 56 Dunedin 9054 New Zealand Tel 64 3 479 8269 Fax 64 3 479 8279 Email human.resources@otago.ac.nz"}, "https://otago.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=2601474": {"title": "Communications Advisor (M\u0101ori)", "description": "Job Description - Communications Advisor (M\u0101ori) (2601474) Go to the main content section. Human Resources Information for Staff Working @ Otago Join Otago About Otago University Application toolkit Living & working in New Zealand Career development & training Health & Safety HR toolkit HR policies Contacts & enquiries Current Vacancies Otago staff should use the internal version Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Jobs | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Job Page Basic Search | Advanced Search | Jobs Matching My Profile | All Jobs Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Communications Advisor (M\u0101ori) (2601474) Communications Advisor (M\u0101ori) - 2601474 __________ COMMUNICATION SERVICES | RATONGA P\u0100RONGORONGO EXTERNAL ENGAGEMENT DIVISION | TE RINGA TORO Who we are | Ko wai m\u0101tou He aha te mea nui \u014d te ao? He tangata, he tangata, he tangata! The University of Otago \u2013 \u014ct\u0101kou Whakaihu Waka is blessed with staff, students and community partners who are dedicated to M\u0101ori aspirations in Aotearoa. As well as celebrating M\u0101ori students, we are committed to enhancing the visibility of our teaching, research, and community engagement through a range of communications and other promotional activities. Ranked within the top 1% of universities in the world, \u014ct\u0101kou Whakaihu Waka has a strong national and international reputation and a firm commitment to enhance our relationship with mana whenua through our M\u0101ori Strategic Framework. Our purpose in Communications is to connect the University, internally and externally. We use a range of communications tools and channels to provide information to our audiences which: enhance and protect the University\u2019s reputation; raises its profile; and attracts quality students and external funding. Our members are highly experienced communicators from a range of backgrounds with a strong and positive team culture. The role | Te mahi Reporting directly to the Manager Media Engagement, our Kaitohutohu P\u0101p\u0101ho M\u0101ori will work across the University, and promote the incorporation and actioning of the M\u0101ori Strategic Framework. This role acts as a conduit between high-level M\u0101ori staff and the wider University community and is an opportunity to inspire the next generation of M\u0101ori achievers to come learn, teach and research with us. You will proactively engage with M\u0101ori media to share stories from the University and collaborate with them to serve their audiences and promote the University of Otago\u2019s key voices. This role has the opportunity to make a genuine difference to M\u0101ori staff and our record numbers of M\u0101ori students and highlight how M\u0101ori can impact the future world from here. Your skills and experience | K\u0101 p\u016bkeka me k\u0101 wheako We are looking for a communications adviser who is: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0A strong writer. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Has an in-depth knowledge of tikanga M\u0101ori. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Has existing experience or a desire to develop a career in communications. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Can demonstrate the skills needed for strong stakeholder engagement. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0A relevant qualification in communications, public relations, or journalism. Preference will be given to someone who has: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Strong te reo M\u0101ori proficiency. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Experience in communications, journalism, or public relations. You will be an articulate and engaging communicator, with a strong customer service orientation and sense of team spirit. Further details | P\u016broko We are seeking to fill one permanent, part-time position (30 hours a week), based in \u014ctepoti, Dunedin The appointment range for this role is $80,749 to $85,649 per annum (pro-rata). Top of the range is $100,776 (pro-rata). We offer competitive salary, 5 weeks\u2019 annual leave, a 6.75% superannuation scheme, and the ability to achieve real work/life balance. You must have the right to live and work in New Zealand to apply for this position. For further information, or to discuss the role in confidence \u2013 please contact Sarah Milne, Manager Media Engagement, via the contact details below. Application | Tono To submit your application including CV and cover letter, please click the apply button below. Applications quoting reference number 2601474 will close on Wednesday, 28 October 2026. Applications may be reviewed as submitted. The University reserves the right to close this vacancy at any time. Additional Information Note: As a part-time position, the salary range for this role will be the pro-rata equivalent of the annual full-time salary range listed. Contact: Sarah Milne Position details: Job Description Further Information: Department Website Create an email with a link to this vacancy: Create email Location: About Dunedin Primary Location NZL-SI-Dunedin Employment Status Permanent Salary Level and Range Level 7 (Range of Appointments $80,749 to $85,649, Top of Range $100,776) Organisation Director's Office, Communications Job Function Marketing and Public Relations ^ Top of page | Accessibility | Copyright & Disclaimer | Contact Us | Feedback | Top of page \u00a9 Human Resources 1st Floor Registry Building PO Box 56 Dunedin 9054 New Zealand Tel 64 3 479 8269 Fax 64 3 479 8279 Email human.resources@otago.ac.nz"}, "https://otago.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=2601469": {"title": "Joint Clinical; Senior Lecturer and Consultant in Obstetrics & Gynaecology", "description": "Job Description - Joint Clinical; Senior Lecturer and Consultant in Obstetrics & Gynaecology (2601469) Go to the main content section. Human Resources Information for Staff Working @ Otago Join Otago About Otago University Application toolkit Living & working in New Zealand Career development & training Health & Safety HR toolkit HR policies Contacts & enquiries Current Vacancies Otago staff should use the internal version Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Jobs | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Job Page Basic Search | Advanced Search | Jobs Matching My Profile | All Jobs Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Joint Clinical; Senior Lecturer and Consultant in Obstetrics & Gynaecology (2601469) Joint Clinical; Senior Lecturer and Consultant in Obstetrics & Gynaecology - 2601469 __________ DEPARTMENT OF OBSTETRICS AND GYNAECOLOGY | ORANGA W\u0100HINE FACULTY OF MEDICINE - DUNEDIN, UNIVERSITY OF OTAGO | TE KAUPEKA WHAIORA - \u014cTEPOTI, \u014cT\u0100KOU WHAKAIHU WAKA and HEALTH NEW ZEALAND | TE WHATU ORA SOUTHERN The Department of Obstetrics and Gynaecology (O&G) | Oranga W\u0101hine, University of Otago, in partnership with Health New Zealand | Te Whatu Ora Southern, invites applications for an outstanding clinical academic to join our team in a joint clinical appointment (0.8 FTE) with clinical care focused on Early Pregnancy and Abortion Care. Drawing on the strengths of one of Australasia's leading medical schools and a progressive regional health service, this position offers a unique opportunity to influence clinical service delivery, education, research, and workforce development across Aotearoa New Zealand. The Role | Te Mahi This joint appointment combines: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a00.5 FTE Academic Component as Senior Lecturer with the University of Otago. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a00.3 FTE Clinical Component as an O&G specialist with a special interest in Abortion care with Health New Zealand | Te Whatu Ora Southern. As a clinical academic, you will provide leadership in teaching, research, and service development while delivering specialist clinical care with a focus on abortion and early pregnancy. You will contribute to the advancement of equitable women's health outcomes through education, research, quality improvement, and culturally safe clinical practice guided by Te Tiriti o Waitangi. Academic Responsibilities Based within the Department of Obstetrics and Gynaecology | Oranga W\u0101hine, you will: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Deliver high-quality undergraduate and postgraduate teaching. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Contribute to curriculum development, assessment, and paper coordination. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Supervise postgraduate research students. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Develop a strong research profile through publication, external funding, and collaboration. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Work collaboratively across the Faculty of Medicine and support the University's commitment to Pae Tata and the M\u0101ori Strategic Framework. Clinical Responsibilities Working within the Women's Health Service at Dunedin Hospital, you will: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Provide patient-centred, evidence-based abortion and early pregnancy services. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Deliver comprehensive sexual and reproductive healthcare, including contraception and counselling. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Contribute to leadership, service development, quality improvement, and clinical governance. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Support regional service provision across Otago, Southland, and wider Southern communities. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Provide education and supervision for medical and nursing staff, while maintaining high standards of clinical care consistent with RANZCOG, Medical Council of New Zealand, and Health New Zealand requirements. Your Skills and Experience | K\u0101 P\u016bkeka me K\u0101 Wheako The successful applicant will have: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Specialist qualifications recognised by RANZCOG (or equivalent) and recognised by the Medical Council of New Zealand. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Eligibility for vocational registration in New Zealand. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Experience and expertise in sexual and reproductive health, abortion care, and early pregnancy care. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0A commitment to culturally safe practice and the principles of Te Tiriti o Waitangi. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Experience in undergraduate and/or postgraduate teaching. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Demonstrated research achievement or clear potential to establish a productive research programme. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Excellent communication, collaboration, and leadership skills. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0A commitment to quality improvement, education, and workforce development. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0The ability to work effectively within multidisciplinary teams. Desirable: A higher research degree (PhD or equivalent), experience in service leadership and clinical governance, a strong research track record, and expertise in developing sexual and reproductive health services and models of care. About Our Team | M\u014d Te T\u012bma The Department of Obstetrics and Gynaecology | Oranga W\u0101hine is committed to advancing obstetric, gynaecological, sexual reproductive and women's health through excellence in education, research, and clinical care. We play a major role in the six-year MBChB programme and offer a range of postgraduate qualifications and research opportunities, including Masters and PhD supervision. Health New Zealand | Te Whatu Ora Southern serves a population of approximately 350,000 people across New Zealand's largest geographical health region. Our services are delivered through strong multidisciplinary partnerships committed to equity, innovation, and exceptional patient care. Why join us? | He aha ai m\u0101tou? This role offers the opportunity to: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Shape the future of sexual and reproductive healthcare in Aotearoa. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Develop a rewarding academic and clinical career within a highly respected institution. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Work alongside nationally recognised clinicians and researchers. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Lead innovation in early pregnancy and abortion care. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Enjoy the lifestyle benefits of living in \u014ctepoti Dunedin, a vibrant university city renowned for its natural environment, cultural offerings, and excellent work-life balance. Further details | P\u016broko This is a permanent joint clinical appointment (0.8 FTE total comprising 0.5 FTE academic and 0.3 FTE clinical duties) based in \u014ctepoti, Dunedin. The University of Otago and Health New Zealand | Te Whatu Ora are committed to equity, diversity, inclusion, and honouring Te Tiriti o Waitangi. We welcome applications from candidates who will contribute to our diverse and inclusive community. For a confidential discussion about the role, please contact Farai Madambi, Senior Recruitment Consultant, via the email below. Application | Tono Candidates are requested to submit: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Curriculum Vitae. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Cover Letter. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Contact details of three referees. To submit your application, please click the apply button below. Applications quoting reference number 2601469 will close on Sunday, 8 November 2026. Additional Information Contact: Farai Madambi Position details: Information Statement - University of Otago and Information Statement - Te Whatu Ora Guidelines for Academic Positions: Guidelines Further Information: Department Website Create an email with a link to this vacancy: Create email Location: About Dunedin Primary Location NZL-SI-Dunedin Employment Status Permanent Salary Level and Range The University is offering a remuneration level commensurate with the responsibilities of the position. Organisation Obstetrics and Gynaecology Job Function Teaching ^ Top of page | Accessibility | Copyright & Disclaimer | Contact Us | Feedback | Top of page \u00a9 Human Resources 1st Floor Registry Building PO Box 56 Dunedin 9054 New Zealand Tel 64 3 479 8269 Fax 64 3 479 8279 Email human.resources@otago.ac.nz"}, "https://otago.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=2601439": {"title": "Teaching Fellow", "description": "Job Description - Teaching Fellow - Gender Studies (2601439) Go to the main content section. Human Resources Information for Staff Working @ Otago Join Otago About Otago University Application toolkit Living & working in New Zealand Career development & training Health & Safety HR toolkit HR policies Contacts & enquiries Current Vacancies Otago staff should use the internal version Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Jobs | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Job Page Basic Search | Advanced Search | Jobs Matching My Profile | All Jobs Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Teaching Fellow - Gender Studies (2601439) Teaching Fellow - Gender Studies - 2601439 __________ SOCIOLOGY, GENDER STUDIES AND CRIMINOLOGY | TE TAURA TAKATA DIVISION OF HUMANITIES | TE KETE ARONUI Who we are/Ko wai m\u0101tou Gender Studies within the Sociology, Gender Studies and Criminology Programme, is the largest academic unit in the School of Social Sciences at the University of Otago. We are seeking a Teaching Fellow to join our team in April 2027 in a full-time, permanent position. Gender Studies at Otago is Aotearoa New Zealand's leading programme in the field, with an interdisciplinary focus on gender and sexuality in contemporary and historical contexts. We are looking to continue our strengths in teaching gender and the media while growing into such areas as critical technology studies, critical disability and health studies. We offer undergraduate and postgraduate qualifications in Gender Studies and are committed to supporting learning through te ao M\u0101ori and Pacific worldviews. We are actively strengthening our curriculum and research in m\u0101tauranga M\u0101ori and Pacific knowledges and are committed to upholding Te Tiriti o Waitangi and the University's M\u0101ori and Pacific Strategic Frameworks. For further information please see our Gender Studies subject page: https://www.otago.ac.nz/courses/subjects/gender-studies and our Sociology, Gender Studies and Criminology Programme website: https://www.otago.ac.nz/sgc The role/Te mahi We are seeking a Teaching Fellow to join our Gender Studies team. The successful candidate will contribute to teaching across our undergraduate programme, including GEND101: Gender in Everyday Life and GEND205/305: Gender and the Media. The successful candidate will work together with Gender Studies staff, taking responsibility for coordinating papers, delivering lectures and tutorials, coordinating tutors, marking internal assessment and final exams, developing course material, paper administration and management, and coordinating with other staff members for team-taught papers. The successful candidate will have opportunities to grow Gender Studies by developing undergraduate and postgraduate teaching. The role will also include supervising postgraduate research projects, as well as providing pastoral care and course advice to Gender Studies students at all levels. Your skills and experience/K\u0101 p\u016bkeka me k\u0101 wheako The successful candidate will be expected to have: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0A postgraduate qualification (PhD preferred) in Gender Studies or a cognate discipline with a focus on gender. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Demonstrated expertise in Gender & Media, as well as additional expertise in one or more areas of Gender & Disability/Health/Technology. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0A track record of teaching excellence at the tertiary level. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Some experience of postgraduate supervision and/or mentorship. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Evidence of an ability to work with students and staff from differing academic and cultural backgrounds and at all levels of the institution. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0A commitment to contribute to teaching and learning environments that support engagement of students and staff with te ao M\u0101ori, te reo M\u0101ori, m\u0101tauranga M\u0101ori, and Pacific knowledges. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0The ability to contribute to the teaching, postgraduate and research culture, and growth of Gender Studies at Otago. Further details/P\u016broko This is a full-time (1.0FTE) permanent position, based in \u014ctepoti, Dunedin. The appointment range is $75,727 to $102,900 per annum (TFP1-01 to TFP2-05). \u014ct\u0101kou Whakaihu Waka | University of Otago is a workplace that values and utilises diverse and inclusive thinking, people, and behaviours. We welcome the contributions of staff with diverse backgrounds, experiences, skills, and perspectives. Specific enquiries may be directed to Associate Professor Bryndl Hohmann-Marriott, Head of Sociology, Gender Studies and Criminology via the contact details below. Application/Tono Candidates are required to provide: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0A CV, including employment history. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0A letter of application that highlights how your skills and experience address the role requirements. Please include evidence of your teaching quality in your letter. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a03-4 referee contact details, including telephone number and email address. To submit your application please click the apply button below. Applications quoting reference number 2601439 will close on Sunday, 8 November 2026. Additional Information Contact: Associate Professor Bryndl Hohmann-Marriott Position details: Information Statement Guidelines for Academic Positions: Guidelines Further Information: Department Website Create an email with a link to this vacancy: Create email Location: About Dunedin Primary Location NZL-SI-Dunedin Employment Status Permanent Salary Level and Range Teaching & Professional Practice Fellow 1 ($75,727 to $87,849) or 2 ($91,614 to $102,900) Organisation Sociology, Gender Studies and Criminology Job Function Teaching ^ Top of page | Accessibility | Copyright & Disclaimer | Contact Us | Feedback | Top of page \u00a9 Human Resources 1st Floor Registry Building PO Box 56 Dunedin 9054 New Zealand Tel 64 3 479 8269 Fax 64 3 479 8279 Email human.resources@otago.ac.nz"}, "https://otago.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=2601487": {"title": "Executive Assistant (Wellington)", "description": "Job Description - Executive Assistant (Wellington) (2601487) Go to the main content section. Human Resources Information for Staff Working @ Otago Join Otago About Otago University Application toolkit Living & working in New Zealand Career development & training Health & Safety HR toolkit HR policies Contacts & enquiries Current Vacancies Otago staff should use the internal version Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Jobs | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Job Page Basic Search | Advanced Search | Jobs Matching My Profile | All Jobs Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Executive Assistant (Wellington) (2601487) Executive Assistant (Wellington) - 2601487 __________ DIVISIONAL SERVICES AND ADMINISTRATION | WHAKARATOKA ME NG\u0100 WHAKARITEKA \u0100-W\u0100HAKA UNIVERSITY OF OTAGO, WELLINGTON | \u014cT\u0100KOU WHAKAIHU WAKA, P\u014cNEKE \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Salary + 6.5% Superannuation + 5 weeks annual leave. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Family friendly employer. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Professional development opportunities. The role | Te mahi We\u2019re looking for a proactive, experienced Executive Assistant to support our Senior Leadership Team in high-impact role. This role offers the chance to provide trusted, confidential support while keeping operations running seamlessly, perfect for a polished EA or senior administrator with a strong track record at executive level. This Executive Assistant role provides high-level, proactive support to the Dean and Head of Region acting as the first point of contact and ensuring priorities are managed effectively to support the smooth operation of a large, student-focused academic division. This role is part of the Divisional Services and Administration team, flexibly providing administrative services across the University. A strong customer service orientation and commitment to continuous improvement initiatives is critical to your success. Key responsibilities include: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Providing a responsive first point of contact for the Dean, anticipating needs and triaging requests by urgency. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0High level diary management, correspondence, meeting administration, project assistance and coordination of campus-wide events and activities. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Identifying and resolving issues, taking initiative to implement effective solutions. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Preparing and reviewing high-level communications and documentation, ensuring accuracy and quality across a range of matters. Your skills and experience | K\u0101 p\u016bkeka me k\u0101 wheako The ideal candidates bring exceptional communication skills, meticulous attention to detail, and the ability to excel in a fast-paced, constantly evolving environment. These are dynamic, multifaceted roles that require adaptability, sound judgement, and resilience. We\u2019re seeking candidates who: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Thrive under pressure, confidently navigating competing priorities and shifting demands. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Work independently, taking ownership and driving tasks through to completion with minimal supervision. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Demonstrate initiative and resourcefulness, proactively identifying improvements and resolving issues before they escalate. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Anticipate needs, staying one step ahead and responding swiftly to emerging challenges. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Bring energy and agility to a complex environment, contributing to a culture of excellence and continuous improvement. About our team | M\u014d te t\u012bma Executive Assistant roles are part of the Divisional Services and Administration Division, a team of highly skilled professionals responsible for delivering outstanding student and staff experiences through high quality, confidential operational management, and administrative services. We are a strong supportive whakawhanaungatanga, (community), proud of the work we do as the largest workforce in the university, spanning every corner of the motu. Further details | P\u016broko This is a full-time (37.5 hours), permanent position, located in P\u014dneke, Wellington. The appointment range for this role is $75,631 to $80,503 per annum. Top of the range is $87,750. You must have the right to live and work in New Zealand to apply for this position The University of Otago is a workplace that values and utilises diverse and inclusive thinking, people, and behaviours. This means that we honour Te Tiriti o Waitangi and that the contributions of staff with diverse backgrounds, experiences, skills, and perspectives are valued and respected. For further information, or to discuss this role in confidence \u2013 please contact Olivia Fuller for the role via the contact details below. Application | Tono To submit your application (including CV and cover letter) please click the apply button. Applications quoting reference number 2601487 will close on Sunday 25 October 2026. Applications may be reviewed as submitted and candidates may be invited to interview immediately. The University reserves the right to close this vacancy at any time. Additional Information Contact: Olivia Fuller Position details: Job Description Further Information: Department Website Create an email with a link to this vacancy: Create email Location: About Wellington Primary Location NZL-NI-Wellington Employment Status Permanent Salary Level and Range Level 6 (Range of Appointments $75,631 to $80,503, Top of Range $88,750) Organisation Divisional Services and Administration (UOW) Job Function Administrative ^ Top of page | Accessibility | Copyright & Disclaimer | Contact Us | Feedback | Top of page \u00a9 Human Resources 1st Floor Registry Building PO Box 56 Dunedin 9054 New Zealand Tel 64 3 479 8269 Fax 64 3 479 8279 Email human.resources@otago.ac.nz"}}, "rows": {"https://otago.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600772": {"school_id": 1826, "posting_url": "https://otago.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600772", "job_title_in_post": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer/Associate Professor", "position_type": "Associate_Professor; Lecturer", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "Faculty of Dentistry is based", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://otago.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600967": {"school_id": 1826, "posting_url": "https://otago.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600967", "job_title_in_post": "Graduate Dentist Intern (Dunedin/Auckland)", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "Faculty of Dentistry, University of Otago", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://otago.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=2501589": {"school_id": 1826, "posting_url": "https://otago.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=2501589", "job_title_in_post": "Senior Professional Practice Fellow", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor; Associate_Professor; Full_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "Faculty of Dentistry is based", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://otago.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=2601312": {"school_id": 1826, "posting_url": "https://otago.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=2601312", "job_title_in_post": "Senior Teaching Fellow", "position_type": "Lecturer", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "Department of Psychological Medicine", "area_key_words": "Fellow", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://otago.ta